.TH GZIP 1.SH NAMEgzip \- compress and expand files.SH SYNOPSIS\fBgzip\fR[\-acdfhlLnqrtvV19] [\-S suffix] [file ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBgzip\fRis GNU gzip 1.2.2.  It replaces each file named with a compressed copyending in\fB.gz\fR,\fRor with\fB\-d\fRturns a\fB.gz\fRfile back into the original.  With no file it reads the standard inputand writes the standard output..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-d\fRdecompress..TP 12\fB\-c\fRwrite to the standard output and leave the file alone..TP 12\fB\-l\fRlist a\fB.gz\fRfile: compressed and uncompressed sizes, ratio and name..TP 12\fB\-t\fRtest a\fB.gz\fRfile's integrity..TP 12\fB\-1 \fRto\fB \-9\fRfaster, or smaller..TP 12\fB\-f\fRoverwrite an output file that exists..TP 12\fB\-r\fRwork through directories..TP 12\fB\-S\fI .suf\fRuse\fI.suf\fRinstead of\fB.gz\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-n\fRdo not save or restore the original name..TP 12\fB\-a\fRtext: convert line ends to the local convention..TP 12\fB\-q, \-v\fRquiet, or verbose..TP 12\fB\-V, \-L\fRthe version, or the licence..SH EXAMPLES.nfgzip notes              notes.gz, and notes is gonegzip -l notes.gz        the sizes insidegzip -dc notes.gz       read it without expanding the file.fi.SH OTHER BUILDS\fBREBUILT/gzip68k_csl ,\fR\fBgzip020_csl\fRand\fBgzipcpu32k_csl\fRare gzip 1.2.4 built for the 68000, the 68020 and the CPU32.  They readand write the same files and take the same options, with\fB\-N\fRto save the original name and time and without\fB\-a\fRand\fB\-r\fR.\fRThey need Microware's\fBcsl\fRmodule where this one needs\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR\fBDOC/README-ARCHIVERS\fRcompares it with the other packers here..SH SEE ALSOcompress, zip, lha